borhood Library Stop","subtitle":"Boylston Street corridor · Chinatown Branch Library","notes":"Step into the Boylston Street branch to read, work, ask library staff for help, or check its calendar for a public program.","short_summary":"A compact Boston Public Library branch at the Boylston Street entrance to Chinatown.","evidence_claim":"Boston Public Library lists its Chinatown Branch at 2 Boylston Street and publishes recurring public hours and an events calendar for the location.","source_url":"https://www.bpl.org/locations/chinatown/","source_title":"Chinatown | Boston Public Library","source_kind":"government","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":42.3524,"longitude":-71.0631,"maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Boston+Public+Library+Chinatown+Branch+2+Boylston+Street+Boston+MA","access_notes":"Current posted hours vary by weekday; the official page lists Saturday and Sunday as closed.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"chin-park-beach-street","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Auntie Kay and Uncle Frank Chin Park","title":"Follow the Serpentine Path","subtitle":"Beach Street corridor · Chin Park on The Greenway","notes":"Approach from Beach Street and follow Chin Park’s curving path through the Greenway’s Chinatown gateway landscape.","short_summary":"A named Greenway park connecting Beach Street with Chinatown through a curving pedestrian landscape.","evidence_claim":"The Greenway Conservancy’s official self-guided tour maps Auntie Kay and Uncle Frank Chin Park beside Beach Street and identifies its Serpentine Path.","source_url":"https://www.rosekennedygreenway.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/11/SelfGuidedTours_Packet-Updated112024.pdf","source_title":"Rose Kennedy Greenway Self-Guided Tours Packet","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":42.3517,"longitude":-71.0594,"maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Auntie+Kay+and+Uncle+Frank+Chin+Park+Boston+MA","access_notes":"Outdoor Greenway park; consult Conservancy notices for installations, events, or temporary work affecting paths.","cost_status":"unknown","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"old-south-meeting-house-washington-street","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Old South Meeting House","title":"Enter a Revolutionary Gathering Hall","subtitle":"Washington Street corridor · Old South Meeting House","notes":"Find the Washington Street entrance and plan time inside the preserved meeting hall where debates preceded the Boston Tea Party.","short_summary":"A historic meeting hall facing the pedestrian-heavy Washington Street corridor.","evidence_claim":"Revolutionary Spaces lists Old South Meeting House at 310 Washington Street and states that its visitor entrance is on the building’s west side facing Washington Street.","source_url":"https://revolutionaryspaces.org/visit/directions-and-parking/","source_title":"Revolutionary Spaces Directions & Parking","source_kind":"cultural_institution","source_published_at":null,"source_fetched_at":"2026-08-13","latitude":42.3569,"longitude":-71.0587,"maps_url":"https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=Old+South+Meeting+House+310+Washington+Street+Boston+MA","access_notes":"Museum admission and operating hours apply; verify current tickets, hours, and security guidance before visiting.","cost_status":"purchase_required","under21_safe":true},{"subject_id":"massachusetts-state-house-beacon-street","subject_type":"street_or_district","entity_name":"Massachusetts State House","title":"Tour the Commonwealth’s Capitol","subtitle":"Beacon Street corridor · Massachusetts State House","notes":"Climb Beacon Street to the General Hooker Entrance for a scheduled architectural, historical, or legislative-process tour.","short_summary":"The gold-domed state capitol offers an inside look at Massachusetts government from Beacon Street.","evidenc